.gradle/

# **The IntelliJ Platform sandbox, and it lands HERE, not in the module.**
#
# `:vscript-idea` runs its tests in a throwaway IDE sandbox, and the plugin puts it at the root of the
# BUILD — not inside the module that asked for it. `vscript-idea/.gitignore` names it and never matched,
# so a `git add -A` after the first test run swept in 2,258 files and —72MB of caches, indexes and a
# bundled executable.
.intellijPlatform/
out/
*.iml
.idea/
.kotlin/

# **Build output, anchored to the root and to one module deep — NOT `build/` on its own.**
#
# An unanchored `build/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, and `:vscript-idea` has a SOURCE
# own repo that pattern silently kept four source files out of version control, so a fresh clone did not
# compile — it worked only where the files happened to exist on disk. Folding the repo in is what found it.
#
# Two levels, because this is a multi-module build: output lands in `build/` at the root and in
# `<module>/build/`, and nowhere deeper.
/build/
/*/build/

# Alternate build dirs (-PoutDir=...), used so a build can run while the client holds build/libs.
/build-*/
/*/build-*/

# JVM crash dumps
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
